# Rune VM instruction set. Single source of truth.
# Format:  NAME  OPERANDS  DESCRIPTION
# OPERANDS is '-' or a comma separated list of operand names; each operand is
# encoded as a little-endian signed 32-bit integer following the opcode byte.
# Opcode numbers are assigned in order starting at 0 by scripts/gen-opcodes.sh.
# Changing this file requires updating docs/bytecode.md (checked by make check-docs).
HALT          -       Stop execution.
CONST         k       Push constant pool entry k.
INT           i       Push the small integer i.
UNIT          -       Push unit.
CON0          t       Push the nullary constructor with tag t.
LOCAL         l       Push local slot l of the current frame.
SETLOCAL      l       Pop the top of stack into local slot l.
ENV           e       Push slot e of the current closure's environment.
SELF          -       Push the currently executing closure.
GLOBAL        g       Push global g.
SETGLOBAL     g       Pop the top of stack into global g.
POP           -       Discard the top of stack.
TUPLE         n       Pop n values (first pushed is field 0) and push a tuple.
SELECT        i       Pop a tuple and push its field i.
CON           t       Pop a value and push constructor t applied to it.
DECON         -       Pop a constructor value and push its argument.
CONTAG        -       Pop a constructor value and push its tag as an int.
CLOSURE       f,n     Pop n values (first pushed is env slot 0) into a new closure of function f.
SETENV        e       Pop value v, pop closure c, and set c.env[e] := v.
CALL          -       Pop argument, pop closure, and call it.
TAILCALL      -       Like CALL but the current frame is replaced.
RET           -       Return the top of stack to the caller.
JUMP          o       Jump to absolute code offset o.
JUMPIFNOT     o       Pop a bool; jump to o if it is false.
JUMPIF        o       Pop a bool; jump to o if it is true.
PUSHHANDLER   o       Install an exception handler whose code starts at o.
POPHANDLER    -       Remove the innermost exception handler.
RAISE         -       Pop an exception value and raise it.
NEWEXN        k       Create a fresh exception constructor named by string constant k.
BUILTINEXN    i       Push builtin exception constructor i (see docs/bytecode.md).
MKEXN         -       Pop payload, pop exception constructor, push the exception value.
EXNCON        -       Pop an exception value and push its constructor.
EXNARG        -       Pop an exception value and push its payload.
PRIM          p       Invoke primitive p; pops its arguments and pushes the result.
